),array(
 ['Chapter 1. Reading for meaning','Main ideas, details, and sequence','Memahami seluruh alur bacaan pendek serta bukti gagasan utama.',
 'Main idea adalah gagasan utama yang menghubungkan rincian, bukan selalu satu benda yang disebut. Sequence menunjukkan urutan kejadian. Kata first, then, after that dan finally membantu alur. Untuk menjawab, cari bagian teks yang mendukung dan jangan menambah informasi di luar bacaan.',
 'Original text: The class made a reading box. First, they sorted the cards by topic. Then, they wrote clear labels. One label was too small, so they made a larger one. Finally, they tested the box with a partner. The project helped them find cards more easily. Teks berfokus pada proses membuat dan memperbaiki kotak baca.',
 ['What did the class make?','Why did they make a larger label?','What happened after sorting the cards?'],
 ['They made a reading box.','Because one label was too small.','They wrote clear labels.'],
 'Baca perlahan dan tandai kata urutan. Terima jawaban pendek yang maknanya tepat sebelum merapikan tata bahasa. Cerita rekaan, tidak meminta nama kelas atau pengalaman nyata anak.',
 [['The text is mainly about ...',['building and improving a reading box','buying a house','a sports race','a weather report'],0,'The events describe making, improving and testing a reading box.'],['They made a larger label because ...',['the box was lost','one label was too small','the cards were wet','the room was closed'],1,'The text states that one label was too small.']]],
 ['Chapter 2. Listening and checking','Ask when a detail is unclear','Menangkap perubahan informasi lisan dan meminta klarifikasi santun.',
 'Saat mendengarkan, perhatikan tempat, waktu, benda yang dibawa serta perubahan. Pertanyaan Could you repeat that, please? meminta pengulangan. Do you mean ...? memastikan maksud. Jangan pura-pura memahami jika detail penting belum jelas. Jawaban singkat dapat dipakai untuk memastikan pemahaman.',
 'Script for an adult: Our model show is on Friday at ten. We are meeting in the art room, not the hall. Please bring your drawing. You do not need scissors. Dialogue: Do you mean ten o’clock on Friday? — Yes, that is right. Bacakan naskah tanpa menunjukkan teks dahulu; pengulangan diperbolehkan sesuai kebutuhan.',
 ['Where are they meeting?','What should they bring?','How can a listener ask for repetition?'],
 ['In the art room.','Their drawing.','Could you repeat that, please?'],
 'Naskah ini tidak menyertakan audio. Jika hanya dibaca, catat sebagai reading practice. Gunakan akses komunikasi sesuai kebutuhan; tidak memberi nilai buruk karena aksen atau kebutuhan pendengaran.',
 [['The meeting is at ...',['nine on Monday','ten on Friday','ten on Sunday','eleven on Friday'],1,'The script says Friday at ten.'],['A polite clarification is ...',['You must be wrong.','Stop talking forever.','Do you mean the art room?','I will ignore it.'],2,'Do you mean ...? checks the intended information politely.']]],
 ['Chapter 3. A short recount','Past events in a clear order','Menulis pengalaman rekaan lampau dengan urutan serta kata kerja yang sesuai.',
 'A recount menceritakan kejadian yang sudah berlangsung. Awali dengan siapa, kapan dan konteks singkat; lanjutkan urutan kejadian dan penutup. Past tense memiliki bentuk beraturan seperti checked dan bentuk tidak beraturan seperti made, saw, went. Dalam pertanyaan dengan did, kata kerja utama kembali ke bentuk dasar: Did you make ...?',
 'Original recount: Yesterday, Mira made a paper bridge with an adult. First, she folded the paper. Then, she tested it with two light cards. The first design bent, so she changed the folds. She did not use heavy objects. At the end, she wrote what she learned. Ini cerita rekaan, bukan instruksi uji beban.',
 ['When did Mira make the bridge?','What did she change?','Complete: Did Mira ___ a bridge?'],
 ['Yesterday.','She changed the folds.','make; after did, use the base form.'],
 'Anak boleh memakai tokoh rekaan tanpa cerita keluarga. Fokus urutan dan makna, lalu perbaiki beberapa bentuk kata kerja. Tidak perlu melakukan percobaan fisik untuk menulis recount.',
 [['The correct question is ...',['Did she made it?','Does she made it?','Did she make it?','Was she make it?'],2,'After did, the main verb uses the base form make.'],['Mira changed the folds because ...',['the first design bent','she lost her drawing','the room was dark','she bought a bridge'],0,'The recount states that the first design bent, so she changed the folds.']]],
 ['Chapter 4. Plans and invitations','Purpose, time, and a polite reply','Menyampaikan rencana serta undangan sederhana tanpa membagikan kontak nyata.',
 'Be going to dapat digunakan untuk rencana: We are going to display our drawings. Undangan perlu kegiatan, waktu dan tempat yang jelas. Would you like to join? mengundang dengan santun. Penerima boleh menerima atau menolak dengan sopan; undangan bukan perintah. Informasi yang belum ditentukan jangan ditulis seolah pasti.',
 'Original invitation: We are going to share our picture stories on Tuesday at two in the learning room. Would you like to join? Please bring one drawing. Reply A: Yes, thank you. I would like to join. Reply B: Thank you, but I cannot join this time. Semua rincian rekaan; bukan undangan acara sungguhan.',
 ['What are they going to share?','When is the activity?','Write a polite refusal.'],
 ['Their picture stories.','On Tuesday at two.','Thank you, but I cannot join this time.'],
 'Tidak meminta email, telepon, alamat atau mengirim undangan sungguhan. Boleh latihan bersama pendamping. Jelaskan bentuk rencana berbeda dari recount yang sudah selesai.',
 [['They are going to ...',['shared stories yesterday','sharing story yesterday','shares a story','share picture stories'],3,'After going to, use the base form share for the planned activity.'],['A polite refusal is ...',['Thank you, but I cannot join.','Your activity is silly.','You must stop.','I will hide your drawing.'],0,'The reply declines clearly while respecting the invitation.']]],
 ['Chapter 5. Comparing choices','Comparatives with clear evidence','Membandingkan benda berdasarkan ukuran tertentu, bukan menilai orang.',
 'Comparatives membandingkan dua hal: longer, smaller, clearer. Untuk banyak kata sifat panjang, gunakan more, misalnya more useful. Superlatives dapat membandingkan satu dengan kelompok: the longest. Sebutkan aspek yang dibandingkan; larger tidak otomatis berarti better. Hindari menilai tubuh atau kecerdasan orang berdasarkan contoh.',
 'Original data: Card A is 10 cm long. Card B is 15 cm long. Card C is 12 cm long. B is longer than A and C; B is the longest of the three. Namun kartu terbesar belum tentu paling cocok untuk kotak kecil. Kalimat The label is more useful because it is clear memberi alasan kegunaan, bukan hanya ukuran.',
 ['Which card is longer, A or C?','Which is the longest?','Does larger always mean better?'],
 ['C is longer than A.','B is the longest.','No. The best choice depends on the purpose and other needs.'],
 'Pakai ukuran rekaan atau benda aman. Bedakan perbandingan fakta panjang dari pendapat tentang kegunaan. Tidak perlu membeli alat atau merek tertentu.',
 [['The correct comparison from the data is ...',['A is longer than B.','B is longer than C.','C is the shortest.','A is the longest.'],1,'B is 15 cm and C is 12 cm, so B is longer.'],['A correct form is ...',['more clearer','most longer','more useful','usefullest'],2,'Useful commonly uses more to form the comparative: more useful.']]],
 ['Chapter 6. Opinions and suggestions','Because, but, and a useful response','Menghubungkan pendapat dengan alasan serta menawarkan saran.',
 'I think ... menyatakan pendapat. Because memberi alasan; but menunjukkan perbedaan atau batas. Saran dapat memakai Let’s ... atau We could ... . Respons yang baik mempertimbangkan usul, bukan menyerang orangnya. Tidak semua pendapat menjadi fakta; alasan dan bukti membantu pembaca menilai.',
 'Original dialogue: I think we need a bigger label because the words are hard to read. — That could help, but the box is small. We could try a shorter title. — Let’s test both ideas. Kedua tokoh mempertahankan masalah keterbacaan, lalu mencari pilihan yang dapat diuji.',
 ['Why do they want a bigger label?','What is the concern about the box?','What do they decide to test?'],
 ['Because the words are hard to read.','The box is small.','Both ideas: a bigger label and a shorter title.'],
 'Boleh bermain dua peran sendiri atau dengan pendamping. Nilai alasan serta kesantunan, bukan seberapa cepat menjawab. Jangan memaksa anak menyetujui semua pendapat.',
 [['Because in the dialogue introduces ...',['a place','a command only','a reason','a person’s name'],2,'Because connects the opinion to its reason.'],['A suggestion from the dialogue is ...',['We could try a shorter title.','You are always wrong.','The box vanished.','Yesterday was Tuesday.'],0,'We could ... offers a possible action for the group to consider.']]],
 ['Chapter 7. Instructions and messages','Steps that another reader can follow','Menulis petunjuk dengan urutan, kata kerja dan batas aman.',
 'Instructions menyampaikan langkah untuk tujuan tertentu. Gunakan kata kerja dasar seperti write, place, check dan urutan yang jelas. Pesan pendek perlu menyebut apa yang diminta tanpa informasi yang tidak perlu. Kata before dan after dapat mengubah urutan; baca seluruh kalimat sebelum bertindak.',
 'Original instructions: To organise the cards, first read each title. Next, put cards with the same topic together. Then, write a label for each group. Finally, ask a partner to check the labels. Message: Please check the blue label before you put the cards away. Tidak ada kewajiban memakai benda biru nyata; cukup model di kertas.',
 ['What is the first step?','What happens after grouping the cards?','When should the blue label be checked?'],
 ['Read each title.','Write a label for each group.','Before putting the cards away.'],
 'Gunakan kartu besar tanpa alat tajam. Minta anak mencoba membaca instruksi buatan sendiri seolah pembaca baru, lalu mencari langkah yang kurang jelas. Jangan mengirim pesan ke akun orang lain.',
 [['After grouping the cards, the next step is ...',['throwing them away','writing a label for each group','closing every book','cutting the table'],1,'The instructions place label writing after grouping the cards.'],['Before you put the cards away means ...',['sesudah kartu disimpan','tanpa memeriksa kartu','sebelum kartu disimpan','ketika semua selesai kemarin'],2,'Before menunjukkan bahwa pemeriksaan dilakukan lebih dahulu.']]],
 ['Chapter 8. Presenting a project','Draft, feedback, and revision','Menyampaikan hasil sederhana serta memperbaiki pesan berdasarkan umpan balik.',
 'A short presentation dapat berisi tujuan, proses, hasil dan langkah berikut. Gunakan kalimat sederhana yang saling berhubungan. Teks visual harus terbaca dan cocok dengan ucapan. Umpan balik membantu memperbaiki satu bagian konkret. Jika belum tahu jawaban, katakan I don’t know yet, lalu cari informasi dengan pendamping.',
 'Original presentation: Our project is a story box. We sorted six cards and made three labels. One label was unclear, so we changed it. Now the labels are easier to read in our small test. Next, we are going to ask another partner to try it. Teks membatasi hasil pada uji kecil, bukan menjanjikan berhasil untuk semua orang.',
 ['How many labels did they make?','Why did they change one label?','What are they going to do next?'],
 ['Three labels.','Because one label was unclear.','Ask another partner to try the box.'],
 'Presentasi dapat kepada satu pendamping, tanpa rekaman publik. Anak boleh membaca catatan atau memakai cara komunikasi adaptif. Uji teks tidak menggantikan observasi listening dan speaking.',
 [['The project group made ...',['six labels','two labels','one label','three labels'],3,'The presentation says they made three labels.'],['An honest reply when unsure is ...',['I don’t know yet.','I know everything.','Your question is bad.','I will invent a fact.'],0,'The reply acknowledges uncertainty instead of making up information.']]],
